<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthew C. Perry</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Commodore Matthew Perry, Perry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthew C. Perry was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> naval officer who led an expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in 1853 and 1854. Backed by modern warships, he forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> to open Japanese ports through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/convention-of-kanagawa">Convention of Kanagawa</a>. The episode exposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>'s military weakness and contributed to its downfall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry.jpg" alt="Matthew C. Perry" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mathew Benjamin Brady · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Commodore_Matthew_Calbraith_Perry.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
